vatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88808?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/skye","id":88808,"login":"skye","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4ODA4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye","user_view_type":"public"},"assignees":[{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88808?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/skye","id":88808,"login":"skye","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4ODA4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"This is related to https://github.com/google/jax/pull/9118 and has two parts. A colab notebook reproducing the behavior show in the code cells below can be found [here](https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1vsOpMEAn0lKUBjZPOOty4cBLqhgqNsEH?usp=sharing).\r\n\r\n### 1. Arrays with a specific shape created by `jnp.zeros`, `jnp.ones` or `jnp.arange` are always placed on the first device that they were created on\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport jax\r\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\r\nNON_DEFAULT_BACKEND = \"interpreter\"  # Should work with any non-default backend.\r\n```\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# Create ones(1) using the default backend.\r\nprint(jnp.ones(1).device_buffer.device(), \"(should be 'TFRT_CPU_0')\")\r\n\r\n# Create ones(1) in a jax.default_device context with a different device.\r\nwith jax.default_device(jax.devices(NON_DEFAULT_BACKEND)[0]):\r\n  print(jnp.ones(1).device_buffer.device(), \"(should be 'interpreter:0')\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\nOutput:\r\nTFRT_CPU_0 (should be 'TFRT_CPU_0')\r\nTFRT_CPU_0 (should be 'interpreter:0')\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis also applies to arrays initially created within a `jax.default_device` context:\r\n\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# Create ones(2) in a jax.default_device context with a different device.\r\nwith jax.default_device(jax.devices(NON_DEFAULT_BACKEND)[0]):\r\n  print(jnp.ones(2).device_buffer.device(), \"(should be 'interpreter:0')\")\r\n\r\n# Create ones(2) using the default backend.\r\nprint(jnp.ones(2).device_buffer.device(), \"(should be 'TFRT_CPU_0')\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\nOutput:\r\ninterpreter:0 (should be 'interpreter:0')\r\ninterpreter:0 (should be 'TFRT_CPU_0')\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis might be an issue with memoization.\r\n\r\nThis also applies to identical `jnp.array` calls.\r\n\r\n### 2. Passing the module-level default device to `jax.default_device` causes unexpected device placement for all subsequent `jnp.zeros` and `jnp.ones` calls\r\n\r\n**Note: The following code should be executed in a fresh runtime.**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport jax\r\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\r\nNON_DEFAULT_BACKEND = \"interpreter\"  # Should work with any non-default backend.\r\n```\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# If the first array created by jnp.ones or jnp.zeros is created within a\r\n# jax.default_device context that was passed the module-level\r\n# default device, then all subsequent arrays created by those functions will be\r\n# placed on the module-level default device.\r\nwith jax.default_device(jax.devices(jax.default_backend())[0]):\r\n  print(jnp.ones(3).device_buffer.device(), \"(should be 'TFRT_CPU_0')\")\r\n\r\n# Note that ones(4) has not already been created, so this is a separate issue\r\n# from the one described above.\r\nwith jax.default_device(jax.devices(NON_DEFAULT_BACKEND)[0]):\r\n  print(jnp.ones(4).device_buffer.device(), \"(should be 'interpreter:0')\")\r\n\r\n# jnp.zeros is affected as well.\r\nwith jax.default_device(jax.devices(NON_DEFAULT_BACKEND)[0]):\r\n  print(jnp.zeros(5).device_buffer.device(), \"(should be 'interpreter:0')\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\nOutput:\r\nTFRT_CPU_0 (should be 'TFRT_CPU_0')\r\nTFRT_CPU_0 (should be 'interpreter:0')\r\nTFRT_CPU_0 (should be 'interpreter:0')\r\n```\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# Arrays created by jnp.arange are not affected.\r\nwith jax.default_device(jax.devices(NON_DEFAULT_BACKEND)[0]):\r\n  print(jnp.arange(4).device_buffer.device(), \"(should be 'interpreter:0')\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\nOutput:\r\ninterpreter:0 (should be 'interpreter:0')\r\n```","closed_at":"2022-06-15T19:29:30Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88808?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/skye","id":88808,"login":"skye","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4ODA4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.